From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:11:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: preserve active AP links and MBSSID lifetime

Since stop_ap works per link, ___cfg80211_stop_ap() stops one link of an AP
MLD, but clears state that belongs to the interface: the connection owner,
the SSID and the QoS map. The other links keep beaconing with an empty SSID
in NL80211_CMD_GET_INTERFACE and no DSCP to user priority map, until the
next START_AP on some link sets them again.

Since stop_ap works per link, ieee80211_stop_ap() stops one link of an AP
MLD, but turns off the carrier of every AP_VLAN of the interface and clears
interface state: the SSID, the S1G flag and the beacon rate flag. A
4-address station on another link loses the carrier of its AP_VLAN, and
with it its bridge port, whenever any link stops.

ieee80211_stop_ap() stops one link, but calls ieee80211_stop_mbssid(),
which walks every active link of the interface. The stop of one link of an
AP MLD thus takes apart the MBSSID set of each other link and stops the
interfaces of those sets, on radios that keep running.

Keep the final implementation of this responsibility directly; subsequent
repairs listed below are integrated without intermediate replacements.

